1
00:00:00,327 --> 00:00:02,197
(Sheldon:)That's what my
train used to do.

2
00:00:05,699 --> 00:00:08,369
(Bernadette:)Ready to call
tech support?

3
00:00:08,369 --> 00:00:10,939
(Howard:)Give me the number.

4
00:00:10,939 --> 00:00:12,339
(Howard:)Probably wind up

5
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:14,970
(Howard:)talking to some foreign guy

6
00:00:14,976 --> 00:00:18,946
(Howard:)who's reading from
the same manual I have.

7
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:22,680
(phone ringing)

8
00:00:26,053 --> 00:00:27,953
(Raj:)It's my father, you jerks.

9
00:00:32,392 --> 00:00:33,362
(Raj:)Hello, Daddy.

10
00:00:33,361 --> 00:00:34,661
(Dr Koothrapalli:)What did you say to your mother?

11
00:00:34,662 --> 00:00:35,662
(Penny:)Nothing.

12
00:00:35,663 --> 00:00:37,563
(Raj:)I was just calling to check in,

13
00:00:37,565 --> 00:00:39,035
(Raj:)make sure she's doing okay.

14
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:40,463
(Dr Koothrapalli:)Well, after talking to you,

15
00:00:40,468 --> 00:00:43,568
(Dr Koothrapalli:)she seems to think
I'm some sort of playboy.

16
00:00:43,571 --> 00:00:45,041
(Leonard:)Really?

17
00:00:45,039 --> 00:00:48,009
(Raj:)I don't know where
she'd get an idea like that.

18
00:00:48,009 --> 00:00:50,379
(Raj:)You know Mummy
and her crazy imagination.

19
00:00:50,378 --> 00:00:53,748
(Raj:)I'm so lucky I take after you.

20
00:00:53,748 --> 00:00:57,518
(Dr Koothrapalli:)You think you take after me?

21
00:00:57,518 --> 00:00:58,748
(Raj:)Well, I try to.

22
00:00:58,753 --> 00:01:00,383
(Raj:)I certainly wouldn't
be a scientist

